From 38210d08fbaa616163846f69100aeca22a7b11c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Lee <108008609+orthogonaleety@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 11:36:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 314/468] SURFACE: hid: ipts: Fix size of synthesized HID data
 report

IPTS_HID_REPORT_DATA_SIZE is passed to hid_input_report() as the size of
the synthesized data report. It does not account for the report ID (1
byte) and the scan time field (2 bytes) declared in the fallback HID
descriptor, i.e. the report is 3 bytes shorter than the descriptor says.

Since commit 0a3fe972a7cb ("HID: core: Mitigate potential OOB by
removing bogus memset()"), hid-core drops reports that are shorter than
expected instead of padding them, which breaks touch input on devices
using the fallback descriptor (e.g. Surface Book 1).

Fix this by including the report ID and scan time in the report size.

Link: https://github.com/linux-surface/linux-surface/issues/2150
Link: https://github.com/linux-surface/linux-surface/pull/2233
Patchset: ipts

Signed-off-by: Mingcong Bai <jeffbai@aosc.io>
---
 drivers/hid/ipts/desc.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/ipts/desc.h b/drivers/hid/ipts/desc.h
index 307438c7c80cd..972a7697be1fb 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/ipts/desc.h
+++ b/drivers/hid/ipts/desc.h
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
 #define IPTS_HID_REPORT_DATA	    65
 #define IPTS_HID_REPORT_SET_MODE    66
 
-#define IPTS_HID_REPORT_DATA_SIZE 7485
+#define IPTS_HID_REPORT_DATA_SIZE 7488
 
 /*
  * HID descriptor for singletouch data.
